    {
     "tabId": "0f74798a-4dcd-418a-bebc-ec58059a493e",
     "collapsed": false,
     "id": "7a16c959-edad-421e-8382-f98766119d60",
     "gridsterCoords": {
      "w": 12,
      "x": 1,
      "h": 7,
      "y": 21
     },
     "state": "",
     "type": "TextDisplay",
     "title": "How to read this",
     "config": {
      "locationUrl": "",
      "locationFile": "",
      "editorData": "<div style=\"font-family:'Metropolis','Segoe UI',sans-serif;font-size:13px;color:#ffffff;padding:6px 12px\">\n<h2 style=\"font-size:15px;color:#ffffff;margin:4px 0 10px 0\">Resync &mdash; is it rebuilding, and will it finish?</h2>\n\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#ffffff\">A host or disk was lost. Two questions: is vSAN actually rebuilding, and is the rebuild starving production while it does.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"font-size:13px;color:#ffffff;margin:16px 0 6px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #4a5a66;padding-bottom:3px\">Rebuild activity</h3>\n\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#ffffff\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;color:#8fd3ff\">Resync Read IOPS / Throughput / Latency</span> &mdash; traffic vSAN is moving to restore policy compliance. <span style=\"font-weight:600;color:#8fd3ff\">Recovery Write</span> is the same for writes landing on their new home. <b style=\"color:#ffffff;font-weight:700\">All zero means nothing is rebuilding</b>, which is the healthy state.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"font-size:13px;color:#ffffff;margin:16px 0 6px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #4a5a66;padding-bottom:3px\">Guest impact &mdash; the one that matters</h3>\n\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#ffffff\">Front-end latency beside the rebuild. <b style=\"color:#ffffff;font-weight:700\">Resync climbing while this stays flat is a healthy rebuild.</b> <b style=\"color:#ffffff;font-weight:700\">Both climbing means the rebuild is eating production IO</b> and wants throttling or scheduling.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"font-size:13px;color:#ffffff;margin:16px 0 6px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #4a5a66;padding-bottom:3px\">Back end</h3>\n\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#ffffff\">Component Manager latency and congestion, to see whether the disks are coping with the extra write load the rebuild is putting on them.</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin:14px 0 5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#b6c2ca;font-style:italic\">There is no completion percentage or time estimate in these metrics. This screen tells you a rebuild is happening and what it costs, not how far along it is.</p>\n</div>\n",
      "refreshInterval": 300,
      "widgetId": "7a16c959-edad-421e-8382-f98766119d60",
